From: Holodor <noreply@holodor.local>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: check parent chain in clk_is_enabled_when_prepared()

`clk_is_enabled_when_prepared()` previously checked only the leaf clock's
`ops->enable` / `ops->disable` callbacks. On Qualcomm platforms, leaf
branch clocks (such as `disp_cc_mdss_ahb_clk` managed via `pm_clk_add()`
by `dsi_phy.c`) implement `.enable`/`.disable` (`clk_branch2_ops`), while
their root ancestor (`bi_tcxo`, `RPMH_CXO_CLK`) implements only
`.prepare`/`.unprepare` (`clk_rpmh_ops`).

Because `clk_is_enabled_when_prepared()` returned `false` for the leaf
clock, `pm_clk_acquire()` prepared the clock chain at probe time and
`pm_clk_suspend()` only called `clk_disable()`, leaving `bi_tcxo`
prepared (`prepare_count > 0`) across `s2idle` and keeping `xo.lvl`
(`0x300e0`) voted ON in `RPMH_SLEEP_STATE` (`SLEEP_TCS`), which blocked
AOSS/CXSD deep sleep.

Walk the parent chain in `clk_is_enabled_when_prepared()` and return
`true` if any clock in the hierarchy lacks `.enable`/`.disable` so
`pm_clk_suspend()` unprepares the chain when suspending.
---
 drivers/clk/clk.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/clk.c b/drivers/clk/clk.c
--- a/drivers/clk/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk.c
@@ -1417,7 +1417,17 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(clk_enable);
  */
 bool clk_is_enabled_when_prepared(struct clk *clk)
 {
-	return clk && !(clk->core->ops->enable && clk->core->ops->disable);
+	struct clk_core *core;
+
+	if (!clk)
+		return false;
+
+	for (core = clk->core; core; core = core->parent) {
+		if (!(core->ops->enable && core->ops->disable))
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(clk_is_enabled_when_prepared);
 
